PhD position on the effects of incorporation of emotion-sensitive A.I. on politics and policymaking
 We are looking for a PhD candidate to be part of the A.I. Feels interdisciplinary research project. A.I. Feels investigates how the use of emotion-sensitive A.I. chatbots by key politicians and civil servants affects policymaking. The project studies this using different disciplinary perspectives, including political psychology, political communication, human-machine communication, interpretative approaches and the political sociology of emotions.
 As AI chatbots become increasibly capable of expressing and recognizing emotions and emotional appeals, a crucial question arises: how do they communicate emotions on politically relevant issues and what implications does this have for policymaking and democracy? To answer this question, the PhD candidate will work on the A.I.Feels sub-project 1 (SP1) aimed at investigating how emotions are expressed in output generated by chatbots in response to prompts relevant for policymakers. The PhD candidate will investigate how output generated by prompts typically used by politicians and civil servants displays emotional appeals and emotional cues. The PhD candidate is expected to be open to combine both positivist and non-positivist approaches under the supervision of Carolin Ischen and Gijs Schumacher, both specialized in large-scale quantitative analysis and experimental research and Rosa Sanchez Salgado, specialized in interpretivist and constructivist approaches.
 What are you going to do
 You will complete a PhD dissertation based on scientific articles, to be submitted to leading academic journals. Some of these articles will be in collaboration with other team members;
 You will assist with administrative responsibilities related to the project, such as the (national and international) activities of the project, including scientific conferences and networks as well as expert meetings with policy makers and stakeholders;
 You will contribute to the teaching program of the department;
 You will take active part in seminars of the research program group , the department and the Hot Politics Lab ;
 Your primary residence will be within commuting distance of the University of Amsterdam for the duration of the PhD project.
 What do you have to offer
 We are looking for a PhD candidate with the following experience and profile:    
 a completed MA or Research MA in political science, psychology, communication science, computational social sciences, sociology, or one of the related social sciences;
 Knowledge of topics related to emotions and A.I. and training in quantitative and qualitative research methods (e.g. large-scale quantitative analysis, emotion detection), and a willingness to develop additional theoretical and methodological expertise;
 good research skills, as demonstrated by MA thesis or other publications/assignments;
 excellent command of English;
 the ability to work independently as well as part of a team.
 What else do we offer you
 The position concerns temporary employment of 38 hours per week for a maximum term of four years. The initial employment is for one year. The intended starting date is 1rst January 2027. Following a positive assessment, this term will be extended by a maximum of three years, which should result in the conferral of a doctorate.
 You will attend courses offered by the AISSR and the Graduate School of Social Sciences as part of the PhD program. In addition to doing research, publicizing your findings, and participating in both national and international academic events, you will be involved in teaching (roughly 10% of your time).
 Based on a full-time appointment (38 hours per week) the gross monthly salary will range from €3,204 in the first year to €4,051 (scale P) in the last year. The UFO profile PhD candidate is applicable.
 Salary and conditions in line with the Collective Labour Agreement of Dutch Universities.
 We additionally offer an extensive package of secondary benefits, including 8% holiday allowance and a year-end bonus of 8.3%.
 The UvA offers excellent possibilities for further professional development and education.
 In this institute, you will work
