industry:enza:JR104781.description:
Strong seed production depends on reliable field information and practical operational support. In this role as Field Production Technician, you support the production of Leafy, open field and Allium crops by combining crop monitoring with hands-on support in continuous improvement initiatives, producibility projects, trials, plant material harvest and selection, grow-outs and plant sampling. This is how you contribute to seeds of the right quality, at the right time and in the right quantity.
 Make a difference as Field Production Technician 
 As Field Production Technician, you provide broad operational and administrative support to the production team in your region, at the request of the Regional Production Specialist. You carry out field inspections and monitoring where needed, but also support crop continuous improvement initiatives, producibility projects and trials, plant material harvest and selection, grow-outs and plant sampling. You collect, record and report data that helps ensure reliable, high-quality seed production of our Leafy, open field and Allium crops.
 In this role, your work will include:
 Monitoring crops at growers and recording yield, quality, diseases, cultivation activities and weather conditions;
 Entering data into digital systems in a timely and accurate way;
 Identifying deviations from production standards and reporting or escalating them where needed;
 Supporting improvement projects through fieldwork, monitoring, sampling, data analysis and administrative tasks;
 Carrying out operational activities, such as logistical support, plant sampling, grow-outs and quality checks;
 Supporting purity monitoring, PAC analyses and preventive disease monitoring at production locations.
 What you bring as our future colleague 
 As Field Production Technician, you work accurately, practically and in a structured way. You enjoy working outdoors and can easily switch between fieldwork, operational support, data registration and consultation with colleagues and growers. You identify deviations in time and know when to share or escalate information.
 In addition, you have:
 A vocational degree or Associate degree, preferably in agriculture, cultivation, plant science or a similar field;
 1 to 2 years of relevant work experience in seed production, cultivation or agricultural fieldwork;
 Knowledge of crop monitoring and production protocols;
 Experience with digital systems, such as Excel, ERP systems or planning systems;
 Good command of Dutch and preferably English as well;
 Willingness to travel nationally and work in changing weather conditions during the high season.
 Enza Zaden as your employer 
