 As Location Manager, you are an entrepreneurial and decisive leader who knows how to engage and inspire people around a shared ambition. You are comfortable switching between strategic planning and operational execution and feel just as much at home reviewing schedules and budgets as you do among the crops in the greenhouse or field. With your practical mindset, strong organizational skills, and excellent communication abilities, you know how to successfully develop and grow a new location.
 In addition, you bring:
 Bachelor's level working and thinking ability, preferably in Agronomy, Horticulture, or a related field;
 At least 5 years of leadership experience within an operational or agricultural environment;
 Experience with cultivation processes in greenhouse and/or open field environments;
 Proven experience in building, developing, and leading teams;
 Affinity with planning, budget management, and operational coordination;
 A hands-on mentality and willingness to regularly support operational activities on-site;
 Excellent verbal and written communication skills in both Dutch and English;
