 As Assistant Researcher Bioinformatics, you bring a structured and detail-oriented mindset with a passion for working with biological data. You enjoy creating reliable and efficient workflows, while collaborating closely with colleagues from different scientific disciplines. With your strong communication skills, you can effectively translate data-driven insights into practical support for research activities. You are curious, proactive, and motivated to explore new opportunities to improve existing processes.
 In addition, you have:
 A BSc degree (or equivalent) in Bioinformatics, Computer Science, Data Analysis, or a related field;
 Experience working in both Linux and Windows environments;
 Strong programming skills in Python and R, including knowledge of the Bioconductor repository;
 Experience with version control systems such as Git and workflow management systems such as Snakemake or Nextflow;
 Experience with high-performance computing and sequence data analysis;
