industry:enza:JR105394.description:
Een sterk Seed Processing proces begint bij kwaliteit, veiligheid en nauwkeurige uitvoering. In deze rol als Allround Process Operator werk je aan het optimaal verwerken van groentezaden en krijg je de ruimte om je breed te ontwikkelen binnen verschillende processen. Zo draag je direct bij aan de kwaliteit en betrouwbaarheid van onze zaden voor klanten wereldwijd.
 Maak het verschil als Allround Process Operator 
 Als Allround Process Operator speel je een belangrijke rol in het verwerkingsproces van onze groentezaden. Je werkt aan het voorbereiden, uitvoeren en bewaken van verschillende bewerkingen en draagt bij aan een efficiënt, veilig en kwalitatief productieproces. Daarbij werk je samen met operators, teamleiders en kwaliteitsmedewerkers en krijg je te maken met diverse processen binnen de afdeling Seed Processing.
 In deze rol houd je je onder andere bezig met:
 Controleren van binnenkomende zaden op kwaliteit en specificaties;
 Voorbereiden, uitvoeren en bewaken van verschillende bewerkingsprocessen;
 Continu toezien op productkwaliteit, veiligheid en procesvoortgang;
 Verpakken en gereedmaken van zaden voor wereldwijde verzending;
 Flexibel werken op meerdere subafdelingen binnen Seed Processing;
 Samenwerken met interne stakeholders voor een optimaal procesverloop;
 Actief bijdragen aan verbeteringen.
 Wat jij meebrengt als toekomstige collega 
 Als Allround Process Operator breng je een praktische en proactieve houding mee. Je weet je weg te vinden in een productieomgeving en kunt nauwkeurig werken om kwaliteit en veiligheid te waarborgen.
 Verder heb jij:
 Beheersing van de Nederlandse taal in woord en geschrift (Engels is een pré);
 Ervaring met werken in een productieomgeving is een plus;
 Een flexibele en hands-on instelling;
 Teamspirit en goede samenwerkingsvaardigheden;
 Bereidheid om trainingen te volgen en (indien nodig) certificaten zoals heftruck of reachtruck te behalen.
 Enza Zaden als jouw werkgever 
 Enza Zaden is een internationaal familiebedrijf dat sinds 1938 innovatieve groenterassen ontwikkelt. Met meer dan 3.300 collega’s wereldwijd werken we aan groentezaden met een betere smaak, hogere opbrengsten en sterke resistenties. Dat doen we vanuit onze missie: ‘Breeding to feed the world’. Dagelijks eten ruim 480 miljoen mensen groenten die zijn geteeld uit onze zaden, iets waar we enorm trots op zijn.
 We hebben passie voor ons vak en oog voor elkaar. Goede ideeën krijgen bij ons de ruimte en samen zetten we stappen vooruit. Zo blijven we groeien en vernieuwen, als bedrijf én als collega’s.
 Wat je van ons kunt verwachten 
 We vinden het belangrijk dat je kunt groeien in je werk én je goed voelt in wat je doet. Daarom investeren we in jouw ontwikkeling, welzijn en werkplezier.
 Daarnaast kun je onder andere rekenen op:
 Een functie voor 38 uur per week;
 Een bruto maandsalaris tussen € 2.924,33 en € 3.654,13 (Schaal D, CAO Tuinzaadbedrijven) bij een fulltime dienstverband van 38 uur, afgestemd op jouw kennis en ervaring;
 8,33% vakantiegeld en een aantrekkelijke bonusregeling van 7,5% van je jaarsalaris, afhankelijk van je functieniveau en bedrijfsresultaat; 
 25 vakantiedagen, de mogelijkheid om extra vakantiedagen bij te kopen en één betaalde vitaliteitsdag per jaar, met extra dagen naarmate je ouder wordt; 
 Een bijdrage aan overnachtingskosten wanneer je verder weg woont van Enza Zaden. Deze regeling geldt voor medewerkers in dienst van Enza Zaden in Nederland met een woon-werkafstand van meer dan 100 kilometer én een reistijd van meer dan 75 minuten enkele reis; 
 Een aantrekkelijke pensioenregeling, reiskostenvergoeding als je verder dan 10 kilometer vanaf je werkplek woont en een thuiswerkvergoeding wanneer je in overleg met je manager deels thuis kunt werken; 
 Ruimte om jezelf te ontwikkelen via ons Great to Grow ontwikkelprogramma, opleidingen, cursussen en het e-learningplatform; 
 Volop mogelijkheden om collega’s te ontmoeten buiten je dagelijkse werk, bijvoorbeeld via uitjes en evenementen van de Personeelsvereniging en inspiratiesessies en borrels van Young Enza. Ook organiseren we jaarlijks onder andere een zomerbarbecue, kerstmarkt en nieuwjaarsborrel; 
 Aandacht voor jouw vitaliteit en welzijn met gratis vers fruit, de mogelijkheid om gezond te lunchen op kantoor, het fietsplan, sportactiviteiten via enzActive en mentale ondersteuning via OpenUp. 
 Laten we in contact komen 
 Zoek je een carrière die met je meegroeit? Solliciteer dan via de sollicitatieknop. Je ontvangt binnen enkele minuten een automatische bevestiging. Binnen 10 werkdagen laten we je weten wat de volgende stap is.
 Voor deze functie is een Verklaring van Geen Bezwaar (VGB) vereist (wordt door Enza Zaden aangevraagd)
 Heb je vragen over de functie of het sollicitatieproces? Neem dan gerust contact op met: Sarah Hansen, Recruitment Coordinator, via S.hansen@enzazaden.nl  
 Enza Zaden is een werkgever die gelijke kansen biedt en discrimineert niet op basis van achtergrond, identiteit of persoonlijke kenmerken.
 Wil je meer weten over Enza Zaden? Neem dan een kijkje op onze website .

industry:enza:JR105453.description:
As Global Manager Production, you will lead the global seed production strategy and execution for the Mid-Tech Business Dynamic. You will shape and realize our business objectives, build strong production capabilities and lead a high-performing team. In this role, you help ensure reliable seed supply worldwide and support our purpose: ‘Breeding to feed the world’ by delivering innovative vegetable varieties across the globe.
 Make a difference as Global Manager Production  
 As Global Manager Production, you are accountable for the global seed production performance for the Mid-Tech Business Dynamics. This means ensuring the right quantity, quality, timing, and cost of seed production while contributing to the strategic objectives of Enza Zaden. You will be responsible for developing and implementing the production strategy and operational plans for the assigned crop portfolio. Working closely with Business Dynamic leadership, Supply Chain, R&D and commercial teams, you will ensure alignment between long-term business objectives and production execution. 
 You will also represent Production within the cross-functional Business Dynamic team en Crop Segment teams and contribute to the development and realization of strategic plans and annual objectives. In this role, your work will include: 
 Leading and developing a team of production professionals to achieve business goals; 
 Leading supplier performance management in close collaboration with the Global Contract Manager; 
 Ensuring compliance with quality, phytosanitary, IP protection, and regulatory requirements; 
 Contributing to crop strategic plans and preparing business cases for new production concepts and innovations; 
 Leading production topics within the Tactical Seed Supply Team and ensuring effective communication between strategic and operational teams; 
 Monitoring performance, identifying improvement opportunities, and driving continuous improvement initiatives; 
 Actively contributing as a member of the Production Management Team to departmental strategy and execution.  
 You will report to the VP Production and play an active role within both the Business Dynamic team and the Production Management Team.  
 What you bring as our future colleague  
 As Global Manager Production, you are an inspiring leader with strong people management capabilities and a proven ability to lead cross-functional teams in a complex international environment. You combine strategic thinking with operational excellence and are comfortable making decisions based on data and business insights. 
 You are skilled at stakeholder management, thrive in a dynamic environment, and have a passion for driving continuous improvement and business performance. In addition, you have: 
 A university degree (Master's level) in Agricultural Engineering, Seed Production, Supply Chain Management, Business Administration, or a related field; 
 12 or more years of relevant experience in seed production, seed supply chain, or a comparable international environment; 
 Hands on experience in working with cross functional teams and leading your own team; 
 Strong analytical skills and experience working with complex datasets and business challenges; 
 Demonstrated expertise in process improvement and project management; 
 Good understanding of financial management and business planning; 
 Excellent communication skills and proficiency in English and Dutch 
 Enza Zaden as your employer  
 Enza Zaden is an international family-owned company that has been developing innovative vegetable varieties since 1938. Together with more than 3,300 colleagues worldwide, we work on vegetable seeds with better flavor, higher yield and strong resistances. We do this from our mission: “Breeding to feed the world.” Every day, more than 480 million people eat vegetables grown from our seeds, and that is something we are very proud of. 
 We’re passionate about our work and care about one another. Good ideas are given room to grow and together we keep moving forward. This is how we continue to grow and innovate, both as a company and as colleagues. 
 What you can  expect  from us  
We believe it is important that you can grow in your work and feel good about what you do. That is why we invest in your development, well-being, and job satisfaction. Through our Great to Grow development program, our focus on vitality, and activities that bring colleagues together, we create a work environment where you can keep learning and contribute with energy and enjoyment. You can also count on: 
 A position for 38 hours per week; 
 A gross monthly salary between € €7,774.05 and €11,105.78, based on a full-time workweek of 38 hours and aligned with your knowledge and experience; 
 8.33% vacation allowance and an attractive annual bonus program of 15% of your annual salary, depending on your job level and company performance; 
 25 vacation days, the option to purchase additional vacation days, and one paid vitality day per year, with extra vacation days granted as you get older; 
 A laptop and mobile phone provided by Enza Zaden; 
 A company car; 
 A contribution toward overnight accommodation costs if you live farther away from Enza Zaden. This program applies to employees working for Enza Zaden in the Netherlands whose one-way commute exceeds 100 kilometers and 75 minutes; 
 An attractive retirement plan, commuting reimbursement if you live more than 10 kilometers from your workplace and a remote work allowance when working partly from home in consultation with your manager; 
 Opportunities for personal and professional growth through our Great to Grow development program, training courses, workshops, and e-learning platform; 
 Plenty of opportunities to connect with colleagues outside of your daily work through social events organized by the Staff Association, as well as Young Enza networking events, inspiration sessions, and social gatherings. We also host an annual summer barbecue, Christmas market and New Year’s reception; 
 A strong focus on your health and well-being, including free fresh fruit, healthy lunch options at the office, a bike-to-work program, sports activities through enzActive, and mental well-being support through OpenUp. 
 Let’s  connect   
Looking for a career that grows with you? Apply using the application button. You will receive an automatic confirmation within a few minutes. We will let you know the next step within 10 business days.  
 Do you have questions about the role or the application process? Please feel free to contact Esther Scharloo, Senior Recruiter at e.scharloo@enzazaden.nl or call/whatsapp +31 6 25 47 35 44.
 Enza Zaden is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate based on background, identity, or personal characteristics. 
 Want to learn more about Enza Zaden? Visit our  website .

industry:enza:JR105481.description:
At Enza Zaden, innovation in breeding starts with turning data and genomics into practical solutions that create impact in the field. As a Genomic Breeder, you will play a key role in bringing new genomic technologies into our breeding programs and helping breeders make better, data-driven decisions. Working at the intersection of breeding, genomics, data science, and bioinformatics, you will translate complex genetic insights into tools and strategies that accelerate breeding progress. Through close collaboration with breeders and technical specialists, you will contribute to the development of the next generation of vegetable varieties.
 Make a difference as Genomic Breeder 
 As a Genomic Breeder, your primary focus is the successful implementation of genomic technologies within our breeding programs. You will act as the bridge between breeders and specialists in data science and bioinformatics, ensuring that new tools and approaches are translated into practical breeding applications. By combining your passion for breeding with your expertise in genomics, you will help drive innovation and maximize breeding progress across crops. In this role, your work will include
 Partnering with breeders to understand breeding challenges, objectives, and opportunities;
 Driving the implementation of genomic selection, predictive breeding, and other data-driven breeding approaches within breeding programs;
 Analyzing genotypic and phenotypic data and translating insights into breeding strategies and recommendations;
 Ensuring the quality, consistency, and interpretation of genotypic and phenotypic data used in breeding decisions;
 Contributing crop-specific expertise to the development of new methods, workflows, and software together with data scientists and bioinformaticians;
 Leading implementation projects and supporting stakeholder alignment, adoption, and continuous improvement of new breeding technologies.
 What you bring as our future colleague 
 As a Genomic Breeder, you are passionate about applying innovation to improve breeding outcomes. You enjoy working across disciplines and know how to translate complex scientific concepts into practical solutions that breeders can use. With your strong communication skills and breeder-centric mindset, you build trust, influence stakeholders, and create enthusiasm for change. You take ownership, collaborate effectively, and remain resilient when navigating new ways of working.
 In addition, you have:
 An MSc or PhD in Plant Breeding, Genetics, Quantitative Genetics, Bioinformatics, Data Science, or a related field;
 At least 2 years of experience in genomic breeding, genomic selection, predictive breeding, or a related discipline;
 Experience analyzing and interpreting genotypic and phenotypic data in a breeding context;
 Knowledge of modern breeding principles, including genetic gain, selection strategies, experimental design, and breeding KPIs;
 Sufficient bioinformatics and scripting literacy to collaborate effectively with data scientists and bioinformaticians;
 Strong project management, stakeholder management, and communication skills.
 Enza Zaden as your employer 
Enza Zaden is an international family-owned company that has been developing innovative vegetable varieties since 1938. Together with more than 3,300 colleagues worldwide, we work on vegetable seeds with better flavor, higher yields and strong resistances. We do this from our mission: “Breeding to feed the world.” Every day, more than 480 million people eat vegetables grown from our seeds, and that is something we are very proud of.
 We are passionate about our work and care about one another. Good ideas are given room to grow and together we keep moving forward. This is how we continue to grow and innovate, both as a company and as colleagues.
 What you can expect from us 
 We believe it is important that you can grow in your work and feel good about what you do. That is why we invest in your development, well-being, and job satisfaction. Through our Great to Grow development program, our focus on vitality, and activities that bring colleagues together, we create a work environment where you can keep learning and contribute with energy and enjoyment.
 You can also count on:
 A position for 38 hours per week;
 Depending on your experience and background, you will be appointed as a Genomic Breeder I or Genomic Breeder II. The gross monthly salary ranges between €3,984.18 and € 5,500.87 (Scale H, Collective Labor Agreement for Vegetable Seed Companies) for Genomic Breeder I and from €4,356.06 to €6,222.94 for Genomic Breeder II, based on a full-time workweek of 38 hours;
 8.33% vacation allowance and an attractive annual bonus program of 10% of your annual salary, depending on your job level and company performance;
 25 vacation days, the option to purchase additional vacation days, and one paid vitality day per year, with extra vacation days granted as you get older;
 A laptop and mobile phone provided by Enza Zaden;
 A contribution toward overnight accommodation costs if you live farther away from Enza Zaden. This program applies to employees working for Enza Zaden in the Netherlands whose one-way commute exceeds 100 kilometers and 75 minutes;
 An attractive retirement plan, commuting reimbursement if you live more than 10 kilometers from your workplace and a remote work allowance when working partly from home in consultation with your manager;
 Opportunities for personal and professional growth through our Great to Grow development program, training courses, workshops, and e-learning platform;
 Plenty of opportunities to connect with colleagues outside of your daily work through social events organized by the Staff Association, as well as Young Enza networking events, inspiration sessions, and social gatherings. We also host an annual summer barbecue, Christmas market and New Year’s reception;
 A strong focus on your health and well-being, including free fresh fruit, healthy lunch options at the office, a bike-to-work program, sports activities through enzActive, and mental well-being support through OpenUp.
 Let’s connect 
Looking for a career that grows with you? Apply using the application button. You will receive an automatic confirmation within a few minutes. We will let you know the next step within 10 business days.
 Do you have questions about the role or the application process? Please feel free to contact Annemarie Weening, Senior Corporate Recruiter, at a.weening@enzazaden.nl.
