industry:enza:JR105535.description:
As Senior Tactical Supply Planner Mid Tech you translate, together with your team, complex supply challenges into practical solutions that keep our customers supplied and our business moving forward. In this role, you work at the heart of our global supply chain, bringing together colleagues from Production, R&D, Quality and Demand Planning to create the best possible supply plan for your crop portfolio.
 Make a difference as Senior Tactical Supply Planner Mid Tech 
 As Senior Tactical Supply Planner Mid Tech, you lead cross-functional Seed Supply Teams and you are responsible for the tactical supply planning of the global Cucurbit’s portfolio. You ensure that customer service levels are achieved while balancing supply risks, inventory levels, production capacities and business priorities. Working closely with stakeholders across the organization, you lead the tactical supply planning process and help translate data, scenarios and constraints into informed decisions. Your work directly contributes to seed availability for customers around the world. In this role, your work will include:
 Managing and coaching a team of around 3 Operational Supply Planners;
 Identifying supply risks, capacity bottlenecks and inventory challenges, and driving solutions together with Production, R&D, Quality and Commercial teams;
 Preparing and facilitating Tactical and Operational Seed Supply Reviews, ensuring alignment and clear follow-up on decisions and actions;
 Managing supply implications of new product introductions, phase-ins and phase-outs, and ensuring planning systems are prepared accordingly;
 Monitoring inventory quality and availability, managing and coaching Operational Supply Planners and supporting decision-making on seed inventory management;
 Contributing to continuous improvement initiatives and participating in international supply chain projects.
 What you bring as our future colleague 
 As Senior Tactical Supply Planner Mid Tech, you enjoy solving complex supply chain challenges and bringing people together around a common plan. You will coach and manage a small team on “going the extra mile for each other”. You can quickly analyse large amounts of information, identify priorities and translate insights into practical actions. You communicate confidently with stakeholders across functions and levels and are comfortable working in an international environment. In addition, you have:
 A Master's degree in Supply Chain Management, Business Administration, Engineering or a related field;
 Approximately 6 to 8 years of relevant experience within supply chain planning, operations or a comparable environment;
 Strong analytical skills and experience working with complex datasets;
 Experience with ERP systems, advanced planning tools and Excel applications;
 The ability to influence and align stakeholders without direct hierarchical authority;
 Excellent communication skills and fluency in English, both written and spoken.
 Enza Zaden as your employer 
Enza Zaden is an international family-owned company that has been developing innovative vegetable varieties since 1938. Together with more than 3,300 colleagues worldwide, we work on vegetable seeds with better flavor, higher yields and strong resistances. We do this from our mission: “Breeding to feed the world.” Every day, more than 480 million people eat vegetables grown from our seeds, and that is something we are very proud of.
 We are passionate about our work and care about one another. Good ideas are given room to grow and together we keep moving forward. This is how we continue to grow and innovate, both as a company and as colleagues.
 What you can expect from us 
We believe it is important that you can grow in your work and feel good about what you do. That is why we invest in your development, well-being, and job satisfaction. Through our Great to Grow development program, our focus on vitality, and activities that bring colleagues together, we create a work environment where you can keep learning and contribute with energy and enjoyment.
 You can also count on:
 A position for 38 hours per week;
 A gross monthly salary between €5,974.10 and €8,534.42 based on a full-time workweek of 38 hours and aligned with your knowledge and experience;
 8.33% vacation allowance and an attractive annual bonus program of 15% of your annual salary, depending on your job level and company performance;
 25 vacation days, the option to purchase additional vacation days, and one paid vitality day per year, with extra vacation days granted as you get older;
 A laptop and mobile phone provided by Enza Zaden;
 A contribution toward overnight accommodation costs if you live farther away from Enza Zaden. This program applies to employees working for Enza Zaden in the Netherlands whose one-way commute exceeds 100 kilometers and 75 minutes;
 An attractive retirement plan, commuting reimbursement if you live more than 10 kilometers from your workplace and a remote work allowance when working partly from home in consultation with your manager;
 Opportunities for personal and professional growth through our Great to Grow development program, training courses, workshops, and e-learning platform;
 Plenty of opportunities to connect with colleagues outside of your daily work through social events organized by the Staff Association, as well as Young Enza networking events, inspiration sessions, and social gatherings. We also host an annual summer barbecue, Christmas market and New Year’s reception;
 A strong focus on your health and well-being, including free fresh fruit, healthy lunch options at the office, a bike-to-work program, sports activities through enzActive, and mental well-being support through OpenUp.
 Let’s connect 
Looking for a career that grows with you? Apply using the application button. You will receive an automatic confirmation within a few minutes. We will let you know the next step within 10 business days.
 Do you have questions about the role or the application process? Please feel free to contact Esther Scharloo, Senior Recruiter at e.scharloo@enzazaden.nl .
 Enza Zaden is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate based on background, identity, or personal characteristics.
 Want to learn more about Enza Zaden? Visit our website .

industry:enza:JR105569.description:
Reliable seed availability starts with sharp operational planning and strong collaboration across the supply chain. As Operational Supply Planner within our Leafy Team, you play an important role in keeping our global seed supply running smoothly.  In this international role, you combine operational planning with stakeholder collaboration, process improvement and a clear focus on timely seed availability. In this way, you contribute directly to the availability of high-quality seeds for our customers worldwide.
 Make a difference as Operational Supply Planner 
 As Operational Supply Planner, you are part of the Seed Supply process and contribute to reliable seed availability for the Leafy crop group. Using our planning software O9, you review the status of the supply chain, identify risks and bottlenecks, and coordinate the actions needed to resolve issues related to seed availability and quality. Together with and under guidance of the Tactical Supply Planner, you monitor the supply plan, identify gaps and set priorities for product availability and delivery. You work closely with Production, Portfolio, Demand Planning, R&D, Detailed Scheduling and regional Commercial teams to align priorities, solve issues and ensure clear follow-up. Your work helps secure the right seed availability, quality and timing for our customers worldwide. In this role, your work will include:
 Monitoring and optimizing operational supply planning for the Leafy crop group;
 Identifying and resolving issues related to seed availability, quality and delivery timing;
 Supporting the Seed Supply process by preparing input, aligning with stakeholders and following up on actions;
 Collaborating closely with internal departments such as Production, Portfolio, Demand Planning, R&D, Detailed Scheduling and Commercial teams;
 Working with O9 and other planning tools to assess supply chain status, priorities and future availability risks;
 Contributing to projects related to process improvement, process change, strategy implementation and quality.
 In this position you will be expected to work either in Enkhuizen or Voorst, being willing to visit the other site on a regular base. Your manager will be Robert Borsje (Senior Tactical Supply Planner).
 What you bring as our future colleague 
 As Operational Supply Planner, you combine a structural and analytical mindset with a practical and collaborative way of working. You know how to translate complex planning information and large datasets into clear insights and practical actions. With your hands-on mentality, stakeholder focus and sense of urgency, you help the team make timely decisions and continuously improve the way we work. Your have a sharp eye for detail and the ability to keep the bigger picture in mind and you enjoy working in a dynamic supply chain environment. In addition, you have:
 A bachelor’s or master’s degree, preferably in Supply Chain Management, Logistics, Business Administration or a related field;
 3 to 5 years of relevant work experience within supply chain management, planning or a comparable role;
 Strong analytical skills and the ability to work accurately with complex data, planning information and availability risks;
 A structured, hands-on and result-driven way of working, with a strong focus on quality and continuous improvement;
 Excellent communication skills, stakeholder sensitivity and the ability to influence and collaborate across departments;
 Fluency in Dutch and good command of English, both written and spoken.
