wur:16577.description:
Quality Policy Officer
Your job
 Would you like to work as a Quality Policy Officer in a dynamic environment where scientific research focuses on making a positive impact on society? Do you enjoy challenges and variety in your work? Then this part-time position (16 hrs / week) at Wageningen Social & Economic Research could be the perfect job for you! 
 A scientific research institute aims for high-quality work and results. Our quality policy helps us achieve the institute’s strategic goals: delivering products that have impact, meeting the needs of both existing and new clients, and managing risks and opportunities. Wageningen Social & Economic Research is ISO 9001:2015 certified. This ISO standard focuses on risk-based thinking and on identifying and, where possible, implementing improvements.
 To ensure the quality of our research, we work according to various procedures and working agreements. We continuously work to professionalise and improve our processes, and we aim to achieve a high level of client satisfaction.
 As a Quality Policy Officer, your tasks will include: 
 checking, streamlining and keeping processes and procedures up to date, for example through internal audits. This includes processes related to our core activities and their connection with support departments;
 actively working with management and preparing proposals to improve processes and procedures;
 actively communicating about matters related to the quality policy;
 sending external client evaluations and internal project evaluations, and processing the results;
 preparing a draft management report;
 preparing for external audits, including organising them, preparing the content and making sure that follow-up actions are carried out. 
 In this challenging role, you will also contribute to advising on and carrying out various projects related to quality and business operations. Examples include office accommodation projects or the implementation of new systems or procedures.
 In addition, you will work with colleagues from other parts of Wageningen University & Research on quality-related topics. You may also take part in expert groups, where colleagues can share knowledge and learn from each other.
 Your qualities
 We are looking for a colleague with the following qualities and skills, who:
 thinks and works at bachelor level (HBO);
 has strong communication skills;
 preferably has knowledge of and an interest in quality management systems (ISO 9001:2015), or is willing to learn more about them;
 maintains the quality policy and provides management with advice, both when asked and on their own initiative;
 has a strong eye for detail and is able to analyze data and processes;
 is able to identify risks and develop improvement plans based on findings;
 is results-oriented and is good at bringing people together;
 has an excellent command of Dutch and at least B2-level English, both spoken and written;
 preferably has work experience in a research institute or a similar environment, such as a policy organization.
 We offer
 Wageningen University & Research offers excellent  terms of employment . A few highlights from our Collective Labour Agreement include:
 working hours that can be discussed and arranged so that they allow for the best possible work-life balance;
 sabbatical leave, study leave, and partially paid parental leave;
 there is a strong focus on vitality and you can make use of the sports facilities available on campus for a small fee;
 a fixed year-end bonus of 8,3%;
 excellent pension scheme.
 In addition to these first-rate employee benefits, you will of course receive a good salary. We offer, depending on your experience, a competitive gross salary of between €€3,640,- and €5,132,- for a full-time working week of 36 hours, in accordance with the CLA Wageningen Research (scale 9). For this role we offer a contract for 16 hours per week. We initially offer a one-year contract, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and depending on the organization’s financial situation. 
 We encourage development and internal mobility within our organisation. Our recruitment and selection policy sets out the conditions that apply specifically to you as a (former) employee. If you have any questions, we are happy to help.
 WUR welcomes applications from international candidates living in the Netherlands. However, for applicants for this specific part-time position coming from outside the EU/EFTA zone, immigration restrictions apply based on Dutch and EU immigration laws and applications cannot be processed. 
 Important information
 For more information about the position, please contact Brigitte van Oord, Team lead & Secretary Operations, via  brigitte.vanoord@wur.nl 
Questions about the procedure? Get in touch with Edgar Tijhuis, Corporate Recruiter, via  edgar.tijhuis@wur.nl 
 Ready to apply? 
Click on the application button next to the vacancy on our website. Only applications submitted through our website will be considered.
 You can apply up to and including October 5th 2026 . Internal candidates are preferred to apply before September 10th  2026.
 Applications are reviewed regularly. Therefore, the position may be filled before the stated closing date.
 Welcome, safe, and valued 
Wageningen University & Research (WUR) highly values diversity and inclusion because we believe that different insights lead to innovative solutions. We create a work environment where everyone feels welcome, safe, and appreciated, regardless of background, identity, or experience. Together, we are building a culture where everyone's unique contribution adds to the success of our organization.
 We are
 ​The mission of Wageningen University & Research is “To explore the potential of nature to improve the quality of life”. Under the banner Wageningen University & Research, Wageningen University and the specialised research institutes of the Wageningen Research Foundation have joined forces in contributing to finding solutions to important questions in the domain of healthy food and living environment. With its roughly 30 branches, 7,600 employees (6,700 fte) and 13,100 students and over 150,000 participants to WUR’s Life Long Learning, Wageningen University & Research is one of the leading organisations in its domain. The unique Wageningen approach lies in its integrated approach to issues and the collaboration between different disciplines.
