wur:16616.description:
The goal of this research project is to unravel the genetic basis and molecular mechanisms involved in plant defence traits that kill insect eggs, preventing insect larvae from hatching or impeding their development, thereby reducing damage to the plant. Little is known about plant immune receptor genes involved in egg-killing, how insect-derived ligands are perceived, and which immune pathways are activated.
As a postdoctoral researcher, you will contribute to the characterisation of plant immune receptor genes, identify their intra- and interspecific diversity, and investigate downstream immune pathways.
This project is part of an NWP OTP project and executed in close collaboration with vegetable breeding and seed companies. Within the insect team at Biosystematics, you will lead both dry lab (Bioinformatics) as well as wet lab (plant transformation and receptor characterization) activities and co-supervise two PhD students.
 Your duties and responsibilities include: 
 NGS techniques;
 RNAseq;
 Plant transformation;
 Bioinformatic analysis;
 Crispr-cas9.
 Your team 
You will work with Dr. Fatouros and her team, including a postdoc, two PhD students, two technicians, close collaborators at Biosystematics Group, Dr. Klaas Bouwmeester and Dr. Robin van Velzen as well as collaborators of Plant Breeding, incl. Dr. Lotte Caarls.
 You will work here 
You will join the insect team led by Dr. Fatouros within the Biosystematics group at Wageningen University. Our research explores the evolutionary ecology of plant-insect interactions in close collaboration with plant physiologists, molecular biologists and plant pathologists. Research in the Biosystematics group focuses on plant and insect biodiversity and its evolutionary origins, both within and above the species level. The Biosystematics group is part of the Plant Sciences Group at Wageningen University.

REQUIREMENTS:
The successful candidate is an early-career postdoctoral researcher with a PhD degree in Biology/Plant sciences with a specialization in entomology, phytopathology, microbiology or similar, and experience with insect/plant-microbe interactions.
 You also possess: 
 A PhD in Biology/Plant Sciences;
 Work experience in dry and wet lab;
 Knowledge of statistical analysis of large data sets;
 Collaborative spirit;
 Experience in supervision MSc thesis students.
In our international working environment there is an increasing amount of communication in English. For this position it is about language level C1 .

CONTRACT: 1 year

wur:16617.description:
HR Services Officer
Your job
 How do you ensure that employees and managers quickly find their way in the world of HR?  
 As an HR Services Officer, you are an important link in the daily HR services. You help employees and managers move forward, ensure that HR processes run smoothly and see where things can be improved. 
 From a new employee who starts at WUR to a colleague who grows or leaves the company: you ensure that the administrative and organisational side is well organised. In doing so, you have an eye for the person behind the process. For example, an international employee needs different procedures than a Dutch colleague. You know what is needed and quickly find the right way.
 You work closely with HR colleagues and are a reliable guide for managers with a variety of HR questions. At the same time, you look beyond today's question. You identify bottlenecks, think along about solutions and contribute to HR processes that are becoming smarter, clearer and more unambiguous.
 Your tasks and responsibilities as HR Services Officer: 
 providing first-line support to answer questions from managers/employees/HR professionals;
 responsible for the operational process around inflow, throughflow, and outflow within the SLA and process KPIs;
 accepting and handling administrative requests in the field of authorizations and calculations from the organization according to work instructions and process standards;
 ensuring the quality of personnel files;
 takes control and participates in projects in the field of optimization of HR processes;
 you will look for solutions for specific inflow, throughflow and outflow, (complex) cases in which advice is sought from different staff departments.
 you will be responsible for setting up and updating the knowledge base in the HR Services team.
 Your qualities
 You possess:
 HBO working and thinking level;
 3-5 years of work experience in HR Services/HR Support function;
 up-to-date knowledge of HR laws and regulations in the Netherlands;
 knowledge of and affinity with inflow, throughput and outflow processes;
 experience with project-based work;
 you are result-oriented and work accurately, striving for "First Time Right";
 you are a strong communicator and connect at all levels within the organization;
 you show ownership, take initiative and know how to deal effectively with resistance and conflicting interests;
 you have a command of Dutch verbally and in writing. In addition, you have a command of English at B2 level, or you are willing to follow a training course for this.
 In our international working environment, communication is increasingly in English. For this position, it concerns level B2. If you do not yet have this level, we will of course help you and you can contact our language center Wageningen in'to Language. 
 We offer
 Wageningen University & Research offers excellent  terms of employment . A few highlights from our Collective Labour Agreement include:
 working hours that can be determined in consultation, so that an optimal work-life balance is possible;
 sabbatical leave, study leave, and partially paid parental leave;
 there is a lot of attention for vitality and you can make use of the sports facilities available on campus for a small fee;
 a fixed year-end bonus of 8,3%;
 excellent pension scheme.
 In addition to these first-rate employee benefits, you will of course receive a good salary. We offer, depending on your experience, a competitive gross salary of between € 3,381.- and € 4,560.- for a full-time working week of 36 hours, in accordance with the CLA Wageningen Research (scale 8). An appointment of 32 hours is negotiable for tis role. If you have any questions about this, we will of course be happy to talk to you.
 If you are an internal employee, your current contract is the starting point. Ask your HR Business Partner specifically about your situation. We encourage development and mobility within our organization. In our  recruitment and selection policy . You can read which conditions apply specifically to you as a (former) employee. If you have any questions about this, we are happy to help you.
 You will work on the greenest and most innovative campus in the Netherlands, in an international and open organization.
